      "y": 600
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "5f936bfcc1df6004",
      "line_num": 65,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Decide the trial model set and who pays for the tokens. Undecided as of 2026-07-30 and it gates the instance provisioning below. Note the hidden Groq connection on try.sage.is is uncapped per user, and three people will share this workspace.**\n`TODO.md:L65`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 690
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "cd99be70a2131e71",
      "line_num": 66,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Demo tenant reset \u2014 one task, not three. Export School B's KB entries and Agents to a durable destination, then purge them along with their intro-card references, and sweep for stragglers (Space titles, prompt text, uploaded files). A stray reference surfacing mid-demo ends a sales call. Confirm with Alexander whether School B should be asked before their data is removed. This recurs before every demo until Realtor R is off the shared instance \u2014 it is standing overhead, not a checkbox.**\n`TODO.md:L66`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 780
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "f19327970ad30426",
      "line_num": 67,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Day-in-the-life walkthrough \u2014 staged and labelled as staged. The Telegram adapter (`bridges/adapters/telegram.py`, the most mature at 505 lines) carries the demo, but the proactive beats (weather, stretches, reminders) are outbound-on-a-schedule and there is no job scheduler \u2014 the only `scheduler` hits in the backend are the AUTOMATIC1111 diffusion sampler. Trigger the beats by hand, say out loud that they are staged, and show the queue on the roadmap. Do not let \"does it do that by itself?\" get a soft answer.**\n`TODO.md:L67`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 870
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "ff2bf88d548a980f",
      "line_num": 71,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Establish rung one of the responsibility ladder. Nobody knows yet which task comes off his plate first, and the ladder is unbuildable without it. Candidates raised: inbox triage and drafting, listing/client paperwork, follow-up tracking.**\n`TODO.md:L71`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 960
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "3b184d2073eb556d",
      "line_num": 72,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Assess whether documented SOPs exist; if not, introduce TodoScope as the lightweight starting point. This is the input to everything above.**\n`TODO.md:L72`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 1050
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "2366840efe3ce892",
      "line_num": 73,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Map the real system landscape: a CRM, the regional MLS, Google Sheets, Airtable, and a great deal of phone/WhatsApp/memory. There is no single system of record, which means the first build is probably capture rather than integration. MLS access is typically licence-restricted \u2014 establish early whether we may touch it at all.**\n`TODO.md:L73`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 1140
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "cea43b502a4e65ff",
      "line_num": 74,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Settle the WhatsApp question, which is currently mis-framed as \"explore\". The bridge already shipped in 2.0.0 (`bridges/adapters/whatsapp.py`, 291 lines, webhook-driven, HMAC-SHA256 verified, full runbook in `docs/bridges.md`), so there is nothing to evaluate \u2014 the open questions are (a) whether Spaces already covers the internal case and makes the bridge unnecessary, and (b) whether it is client-facing. If it is client-facing on his business number, WAHA is unofficial and carries ban risk on the number his livelihood runs through; that risk conversation happens before we provision. If we do proceed it needs a WAHA sidecar container, a phone number, and a public HTTPS webhook \u2014 try.sage.is is a single-app CapRover deploy with no sidecar beside it, so this is infra provisioning, not a config toggle.**\n`TODO.md:L74`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 1230
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "2711e71b00c43765",
      "line_num": 75,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Establish the brokerage's position on email. Their shared admin and tech staff own it. Any mail-side integration needs their cooperation and may simply be refused \u2014 better to know before it is designed in.**\n`TODO.md:L75`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 1320
    },
    {
