      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 42,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**[WE]** bump `SERVER_TAG=2.3.4` \u2192 `3.0.0` in `distribution.env`. That file is **hardlinked** across AI-UI, homebrew-apps, and Sage.Education-docs \u2014 edit in place with `sed -i`, never with Write or Edit, or the hardlink chain breaks silently."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 43,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**[MANUALLY]** (Alexander) CapRover Method-6 image-pull at captain.try.sage.is \u2192 `try-sage-is` app \u2192 **`ghcr.io/sage-is/ai-ui@sha256:<index-digest>`, pinned by digest and not by tag**. A same-tag redeploy or down/up can serve a stale image from the Swarm cache \u2014 that is exactly what bit the 3.0.0 deploy on 2026-07-16. A verified-good image is not the same thing as a running image."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 44,
          "tags": [
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**[WE]** verify after: `GET try.sage.is/api/config` reports `version: 3.0.0`, `/assets/loader.js` returns 200, and `/admin/diagnostics` renders. Until diagnostics renders, the unresponsive-Agent item below cannot be worked at all \u2014 the tooling for it shipped in 2.3.3."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "c9c63a19a4833131",
      "line_num": 41,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**try.sage.is is THREE releases behind \u2014 2.3.2 live, 3.0.0 is current (re-reconciled 2026-07-30; supersedes the 2026-07-03 two-releases note): `app/package.json` reads `3.0.0` and CHANGELOG's newest release is `[3.0.0] \u2014 2026-07-15`, but `distribution.env` still pins `SERVER_TAG=2.3.4`. The 3.0.0 pin bump was missed, not withheld \u2014 confirmed with Alexander 2026-07-30, no freeze is on record beyond the lifted 2026-06-10 window. Production has never received 2.3.3 (Admin Diagnostics + `EndpointHealth` registry), 2.3.4 (how-to-fix modals + command library), or 3.0.0. This is no longer background reconciliation: a paying customer demo lands on this instance inside a week, so it is task zero and most of the engagement list below is downstream of it.**\n- [ ] **[WE]** bump `SERVER_TAG=2.3.4` \u2192 `3.0.0` in `distribution.env`. That file is **hardlinked** across AI-UI, homebrew-apps, and Sage.Education-docs \u2014 edit in place with `sed -i`, never with Write or Edit, or the hardlink chain breaks silently.\n- [ ] **[MANUALLY]** (Alexander) CapRover Method-6 image-pull at captain.try.sage.is \u2192 `try-sage-is` app \u2192 **`ghcr.io/sage-is/ai-ui@sha256:<index-digest>`, pinned by digest and not by tag**. A same-tag redeploy or down/up can serve a stale image from the Swarm cache \u2014 that is exactly what bit the 3.0.0 deploy on 2026-07-16. A verified-good image is not the same thing as a running image.\n- [ ] **[WE]** verify after: `GET try.sage.is/api/config` reports `version: 3.0.0`, `/assets/loader.js` returns 200, and `/admin/diagnostics` renders. Until diagnostics renders, the unresponsive-Agent item below cannot be worked at all \u2014 the tooling for it shipped in 2.3.3. #critical\n\n`TODO.md:L41`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 710,
      "y": 60
    },
    {
      "color": "1",
      "height": 1150,
      "id": "col-bugs",
      "label": "Bugs",
      "type": "group",
      "width": 300,
      "x": 1050,
      "y": 0
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 657,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Fix the silent-failure footgun**: replace `return None` in all three `generate_*_batch_embeddings` functions with `raise EndpointUnreachable(url, underlying)` so callers see the real cause. This IS Phase 2 of the 2.3.3 hardening plan, applied one layer deeper than originally scoped. See `~/.claude/plans/due-to-the-many-silly-ladybug.md`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 658,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Map `EndpointUnreachable` \u2192 `503` with `{detail, url, fix}`** in a FastAPI exception handler so the UI gets a structured fix-pointer instead of a misleading TypeError."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 659,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Boot probe the embedding URL** so `/admin/diagnostics` lights up red BEFORE the next upload, not at first failure."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 660,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Diagnose sage.startr.cloud specifically**: read the container log for the `log.exception` block preceding a TypeError. Determine which engine is configured (openai? chroma? bare?) and what URL it points at. Compare to try.sage.is's working config."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 661,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Refresh the bug's surface footprint**: the same `Exception \u2192 None` swallow exists in `generate_ollama_batch_embeddings`, `generate_azure_openai_batch_embeddings`, and likely the reranker \u2014 audit them as a class, fix them together."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "b23732b0861fcc22",
      "line_num": 656,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#critical",
        "#bug"
      ],
      "text": "**Knowledge file upload fails with misleading `'NoneType' object is not iterable`: Hit on sage.startr.cloud 2026-06-05 running 2.3.2; try.sage.is on 2.3.2 does NOT exhibit this. The user-visible error is `400: 'NoneType' object is not iterable`. Root cause is downstream of the actual failure: `generate_openai_batch_embeddings` at [retrieval/utils.py:803-805](app/backend/sage_is_ai/retrieval/utils.py#L803-L805) (and the ollama/azure_openai siblings) catches every exception, logs it via `log.exception`, and returns `None`. The caller `generate_multiple` at [retrieval/utils.py:462](app/backend/sage_is_ai/retrieval/utils.py#L462) calls `embeddings.extend(func(...))` \u2014 `None` is not iterable, so the user sees the TypeError instead of the real cause (DNS failure, 401, model not loaded, endpoint not listening, etc.). The real error is in the container logs as the `log.exception` block immediately preceding the TypeError traceback. The try.sage.is vs sage.startr.cloud divergence is most likely (a) different `RAG_EMBEDDING_ENGINE` value (try.sage may be on `chroma` or local sentence-transformer, bypassing this path entirely), or (b) stale URL/key in the sage.startr.cloud DB from the inherited 2-month-old volume.**\n- [ ] **Fix the silent-failure footgun**: replace `return None` in all three `generate_*_batch_embeddings` functions with `raise EndpointUnreachable(url, underlying)` so callers see the real cause. This IS Phase 2 of the 2.3.3 hardening plan, applied one layer deeper than originally scoped. See `~/.claude/plans/due-to-the-many-silly-ladybug.md`.\n- [ ] **Map `EndpointUnreachable` \u2192 `503` with `{detail, url, fix}`** in a FastAPI exception handler so the UI gets a structured fix-pointer instead of a misleading TypeError.\n- [ ] **Boot probe the embedding URL** so `/admin/diagnostics` lights up red BEFORE the next upload, not at first failure.\n- [ ] **Diagnose sage.startr.cloud specifically**: read the container log for the `log.exception` block preceding a TypeError. Determine which engine is configured (openai? chroma? bare?) and what URL it points at. Compare to try.sage.is's working config.\n- [ ] **Refresh the bug's surface footprint**: the same `Exception \u2192 None` swallow exists in `generate_ollama_batch_embeddings`, `generate_azure_openai_batch_embeddings`, and likely the reranker \u2014 audit them as a class, fix them together.\n\n`#critical` `#bug`\n`TODO.md:L656`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 60
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 675,
